    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q2-question-1.svg\" alt=\"During the winter, Ned attends weekly business meetings in Newcastle and always travels to these meetings by car. The probability of being dry, raining or snowing during his travel to these meetings is 1 2 , 1 3 and 1 6 , respectively. The respective probabilities of Ned arriving on time when is dry, raining or snowing are 4 5 , 2 5 and 1 10 . a) Determine the probability that Ned will arrive late for his next winter business meeting. ( ) 5 Ned arrived late for his meeting last week. b) Find the probability that it was raining on that day. ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:580.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q2-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:597.3px\"></figure>",
