      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q2-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(a) The conditional late probabilities for dry, rainy and snowy weather are 1 5, 3 5, 9 10. [B1] [A1] By total probability, P(L) = 1 2 · 1 5 + 1 3 · 3 5 + 1 6 · 9 10 [M1] [M1] [A1] 9 = 20 . (b) The three contributions to lateness are 1/10, 1/5, 3/20, which add to (2 + 4 + 3)/20 = 9/20. The probability of rain and lateness is (1/3)(3/5) = 1/5. [B1] P(rain | L) = 1/5 9/20 [M1] [A1] = 4/9 .\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
