    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q12-question-1.svg\" alt=\"B C 4.8m 3.2m A θ The figure above shows a plank AB resting on a smooth peg. The plank is modelled a uniform rod of weight W N and of length 4.8 metres, resting on the peg at the point C , where AC is 3.2 metres.\" style=\"--madas-width:569.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q12-question-2.svg\" alt=\"The end A of the plank rests in limiting equilibrium on rough ground, where the coefficient of friction between the plank and the ground is 9 13 . 3 The plank is inclined at angle θ to the horizontal, where tan θ = . The points A , B 4 and C lie in a vertical plane which is perpendicular to the ground. Given that the magnitude of the normal reaction of the ground at A is 65N, find in any order … a) … the value of W . ( ) 3 b) … the magnitude of the force between the plank and the peg. ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:578.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q12-question-3.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:590.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q12-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Start with a detailed diagram: Let N be the reaction of the smooth peg: The limiting friction at A is 65(9/13) = 45 N. The angle gives sin θ = 3/5 and cos θ = 4/5.\" style=\"--madas-width:525.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q12-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(a) Horizontal equilibrium gives N sin θ = 45, [B1] hence N = 75 N. [A1] The source also takes moments about A. The weight has perpendicular arm 2.4 cos θ, and the peg reaction is perpendicular to the plank with arm 3.2. Thus W(2.4)(4/5) = 75(3.2), giving 1.92W = 240, W = 125. From vertical equilibrium, W = 65 + N cos θ = 65 + 75(4/5) . [A1] = 125 (b) The force at the peg acts perpendicular to the plank: [M1] Its horizontal component balances friction, giving N(3/5) = 45 [A1] and N = 75 N . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 12 is 6 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "B C 4.8m 3.2m A θ The figure above shows a plank AB resting on a smooth peg. The plank is modelled a uniform rod of weight W N and of length 4.8 metres, resting on the peg at the point C , where AC is 3.2 metres. The end A of the plank rests in limiting equilibrium on rough ground, where the coefficient of friction between the plank and the ground is 9 13 . 3 The plank is inclined at angle θ to the horizontal, where tan θ = . The points A , B 4 and C lie in a vertical plane which is perpendicular to the ground. Given that the magnitude of the normal reaction of the ground at A is 65N, find in any order … a) … the value of W . ( ) 3 b) … the magnitude of the force between the plank and the peg. ( ) 3 "
