    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q13-question-1.svg\" alt=\"C Pulley Pulley A B A block C , of mass 4 kg , is placed on a rough horizontal table, where the coefficient of friction between the table and C is 0.65.\" style=\"--madas-width:562.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q13-question-2.svg\" alt=\"C is connected by two light inextensible strings to two more blocks, A and B , of respective masses 3 kg and 7 kg . Each of the strings passes over two smooth pulleys, each of the pulleys located at the edge of the table, with  A and B hanging freely at each of the two ends of the table, as shown in the figure above. The system is released from rest with the strings taut. By modelling the three blocks as particles, determine in any order the acceleration of the system and the tension in each of the two strings. ( 11 )\" style=\"--madas-width:584.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q13-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Start with a diagram: Take upward for A, downward for B, and towards B for C as positive: [B1] [A1] The available driving force 4g exceeds the resisting friction 0.65(4g). [M1] [A1] With tensions TA, TB,\" style=\"--madas-width:661.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q13-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"TA −3g = 3a, 7g −TB = 7a, TB −TA −0.65(4g) = 4a. [M1] [A1] The table’s normal reaction is 4g. Summing left sides cancels both tensions and leaves 7g −3g −2.6g = 1.4g. Then TA = 3g + 3a and TB = 7g −7a. Adding gives 14a = 1.4g, [A1] hence a = 0.98 m s−2 . [M1] [A1] TA = 32.34 N , TB = 61.74 N . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 13 is 11 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "C Pulley Pulley A B A block C , of mass 4 kg , is placed on a rough horizontal table, where the coefficient of friction between the table and C is 0.65. C is connected by two light inextensible strings to two more blocks, A and B , of respective masses 3 kg and 7 kg . Each of the strings passes over two smooth pulleys, each of the pulleys located at the edge of the table, with  A and B hanging freely at each of the two ends of the table, as shown in the figure above. The system is released from rest with the strings taut. By modelling the three blocks as particles, determine in any order the acceleration of the system and the tension in each of the two strings. ( 11 )"
