    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q14-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Using velocity–time graph: (a) a = dv/dt = 2t −2, [B1] so a(3) = 4 m s−2 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q14-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(b) The velocity factors as (t −6)(t + 4), so the allowed time of rest is t = 6. [M1] The position is x = t3/3 −t2 −24t + C. [A1] From x(3) = 0, [A1] C = 72. [A1] Alternatively integrate just between 3 and 6: Z 6 (t2 −2t −24) dt = [t3/3 −t2 −24t]6 3 = −108 −(−72) = −36. 3 Take the magnitude for distance. Hence x(6) = −36 [A1] and the distance from O is 36 m . [A1] (c) The equation 3x = 0 [M1] factors as (t −3)(t2 −72) = 0. [M1] The nonnegative root other than 3 is √ 6 2 s ≈8.49 s . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 14 is 13 marks.</p>"
