    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q15-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A non uniform plank AB has length 12 m and mass M kg . A smooth support is placed under the plank at the point C , where AC = 3 m . When a child of mass 30 kg stands at A , the plank rest horizontally in equilibrium. The smooth support is next placed under the plank at the point D , where BD = 5 m . When the same child stands at B , the plank again rest horizontally in equilibrium. The plank is modelled as a non uniform rod whose centre of mass is at the point G , and the child is modelled as a particle. a) Determine the value of M . ( ) 4\" style=\"--madas-width:576.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q15-question-2.svg\" alt=\"b) Calculate the distance AG . ( ) 4 Two smooth supports are next placed under the plank at the points C and D , and when the same child stands at E , the plank rest horizontally in equilibrium with the reactions at the two supports being equal. c) Find the distance AE . ( ) 4\" style=\"--madas-width:589.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q15-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Start with a new diagram:\" style=\"--madas-width:566.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q15-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(a) Let AG = x. As AD = 7, [B1] balancing moments about C and D in the two cases gives M(x −3) = 30(3) [A1] = 90 and M(7 −x) = 30(5) = 150 . Expand the two equations to Mx −3M = 90 and 7M −Mx = 150. The Mx terms cancel: Adding gives 4M = 240, [A1] so M = 60 . [A1] (b) The first moment equation gives x = 3 + 90/60 = 4.5 m . [M1] Use the first moment equation [M1] substitute the calculated mass [A1] obtain the distance from the support [A1] express the distance from A\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-o/q15-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"(c) The reactions must each be 45g, since the total mass is 90 kg. [B1] Write AE = y. [A1] Moments about A give 45g(3 + 7) = 60g(4.5) + 30gy, [A1] so AE = 6 m . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 15 is 12 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "A non uniform plank AB has length 12 m and mass M kg . A smooth support is placed under the plank at the point C , where AC = 3 m . When a child of mass 30 kg stands at A , the plank rest horizontally in equilibrium. The smooth support is next placed under the plank at the point D , where BD = 5 m . When the same child stands at B , the plank again rest horizontally in equilibrium. The plank is modelled as a non uniform rod whose centre of mass is at the point G , and the child is modelled as a particle. a) Determine the value of M . ( ) 4 b) Calculate the distance AG . ( ) 4 Two smooth supports are next placed under the plank at the points C and D , and when the same child stands at E , the plank rest horizontally in equilibrium with the reactions at the two supports being equal. c) Find the distance AE . ( ) 4"
